[center][size=6][b]SANDBOX ROOM[/b][/size]
[size=4]A clean, up-to-date testing facility for Fallout 4 - reached by holotape[/size][/center]

[size=4][b]Why this exists[/b][/size]
I couldn't find a decent, up-to-date sandbox or "cheater's room" that still works. QASmoke is painful to use (that sky...), and the similar mods I tried were either abandoned or broken by the next-gen update. So I made my own: one interior facility with everything you need to test weapons, armour, builds and enemies - and nothing that touches the rest of your game.

[size=4][b]Getting there[/b][/size]
A few seconds after you get the Pip-Boy (in Vault 111, with an alternative-start mod, or shortly after loading an existing save), the [b](Sandbox Room) Holotape[/b] is added to your inventory. Play it from the Pip-Boy:
[list]
[*][b]Teleport In[/b] - remembers exactly where you are and takes you to the Sandbox Room.
[*][b]Teleport Out[/b] - takes you back to exactly where you were, with everything you are carrying.
[/list]
Console alternative: [font=Courier New]coc SandboxRoom[/font] (no return point that way).

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[b]The main hall[/b] - a three-storey lab in a clean white high-tech finish, with a proper ceiling and lighting. No skybox in sight.
[list]
[*][b]Crafting stations[/b]: weapons, armour, chemistry, cooking, the Automatron robot workbench, the Nuka-World Nuka-Mixer, and a power armour station with three empty power armour frames beside it.
[*][b]Storage that never runs out[/b]: signed sections of lab cabinets. Whatever you take is put straight back.
[list]
[*]Weapons & Ammo - Ballistic Guns, Energy Weapons, Heavy Weapons, Melee Weapons, Explosives, Ammo
[*]Apparel - Armor, Clothing, Headwear, Dogmeat Gear
[*]Mods - Weapon Mods, Armor Mods
[*]Power Armor - Power Armor, Power Armor Mods (next to the power armour station)
[*]Aid - Medicine and Chems, Food, Drinks
[*]Miscellaneous - Junk (and caps), Magazines, Bobbleheads
[*]Every section also has labelled cabinets for each DLC's items: Automatron, Far Harbor, Nuka-World, Contraptions and Vault-Tec.
[/list]
[/list]

[b]Target range[/b] - a firing lane facing four bays walled off from each other, floor to ceiling.
[list]
[*][b]Holographic targets[/b]: blue hologram humans, super mutants and deathclaws that stand still, never fight back and give no XP.
[*]Bays: Single target, Group of five (for area damage), Legendary target, and practice target stands.
[*]Each bay's terminal sets the target type, its health (game default, 100, 1,000, 10,000 or 100,000) and its armour ([i]game default[/i], or [i]none[/i] so health equals exactly the damage it takes).
[*]Killed targets come back a few seconds later, just beside where they stood.
[*][b]Shooting galleries[/b] at two heights over the lane, with stairs, to test from above.
[/list]

[b]The Arena[/b] - through the door under the ARENA sign.
[list]
[*]A lobby of spawn terminals: Base Game, Automatron, Far Harbor and Nuka-World.
[*]Pick a group (Humans, Synths and Robots, Super Mutants, Creatures, Legendaries), pick an enemy, then pick how many: 1 to 10. Each lands at a random spot in the arena.
[*]A large open space with rocks, mounds and dead trees - no buildings - and railed balconies at two heights to shoot from.
[*][b]Enemies stay frozen while you are outside the arena and wake up the moment you walk in[/b] - and freeze again when you leave. They can't follow you out of the arena: step back into the lobby to catch your breath.
[*]"Kill everything spawned" and "Remove everything spawned" clean up.
[/list]

[b]Perks & Stats[/b] [i](new in 1.1)[/i] - through the door under the PERKS & STATS sign on the north wall: six terminals in a row.
[list]
[*][b]S.P.E.C.I.A.L.[/b]: raise or lower each attribute by one, set it to 1, 5 or 10, or set all seven at once.
[*][b]Perks[/b]: every perk chart perk, by S.P.E.C.I.A.L.: add or remove a rank, add all ranks at once, or remove them. "Remove all perks", or [b]Reset[/b] to remove them all and get the perk points back.
[*][b]Perk Points[/b]: add unspent points (1, 5, 10, 25), or take some away.
[*][b]Level[/b]: level up by 1, 5, 10, 25 or 50 - each level brings its perk point. (Levels can't be lowered without F4SE.)
[*][b]Factions[/b]: Minutemen, Brotherhood of Steel, Railroad, Institute - friendly, neutral or hostile.
[*][b]Hostile Groups[/b]: raiders, gunners, super mutants, Children of Atom, Triggermen, the Forged, synths, Rust Devils, the Mechanist's robots, trappers, Disciples, Operators and the Pack - one at a time or all at once.
[*]Story quests can change faction relations again, and turning a story faction friendly or hostile can break its quests: save first.
[/list]

Doors open by themselves as you walk up to them. Enemies can follow you up the stairs.

[size=4][b]Playing fair[/b][/size]
Everything in the room is free. Whether you keep it is up to you: save before you teleport in, and load that save if you don't want to keep what you took.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout 4 (next-gen or old-gen) with [b]all the DLC[/b]: Automatron, Far Harbor, Nuka-World, Contraptions Workshop and Vault-Tec Workshop. (The Game of the Year and Anniversary editions include them all. Wasteland Workshop is not needed.)
[*][b]No F4SE needed.[/b]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Mod manager (recommended)[/b]: install with Vortex or Mod Organizer 2. The installer asks which game you have:
[list]
[*][b]Packed (Next-Gen)[/b]: the current game. Recommended.
[*][b]Loose Files (Old-Gen)[/b]: the [b]old-gen game[/b] (1.10.163, before the 2024 next-gen update), which can't read next-gen archives. Also works on next-gen.
[/list]
Then enable [b]Sandbox Room.esp[/b].
[b]Manual[/b]: copy the contents of [b]one[/b] folder, [i]00 Packed (Next-Gen)[/i] or [i]01 Loose Files (Old-Gen)[/i], into your Fallout 4 [i]Data[/i] folder, then enable the plugin.

The plugin is ESL-flagged (a light plugin): it doesn't use up a load order slot.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Everything happens in its own new interior cell. The mod does not edit any vanilla records, except the navmesh info map that every mod adding a navmesh has to touch.
[*]Load order: anywhere.
[*]Safe to add to an existing save.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changelog[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.1.0[/b] - Perks & Stats room: S.P.E.C.I.A.L., perks, perk points, level and faction relations.
[*][b]1.0.0[/b] - First release.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]
Teleport out first, and use "Remove everything spawned" on the arena terminals if you spawned anything. Then remove the files. As with any scripted mod, uninstalling mid-playthrough is at your own risk - keep a save from before you installed it.

[size=4][b]Consoles[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Xbox[/b]: available on Bethesda.net (Creations).
[*][b]PlayStation 4 / PlayStation 5[/b]: sorry - I cannot upload a version that works. This mod relies on multiple custom scripts (refilling cabinets, doors, spawn terminals, the arena's wake/freeze, the target bays, the holotape) and custom sign assets, and Sony's policy does not allow mods to include their own scripts or assets. A PlayStation version would just be an empty building.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Legendary targets in the target range are the game's own legendary enemies, so they do give XP.
[*]Enemies you spawn in the arena stay until you kill or remove them.
[/list]

